   "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:45mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/pmt/pure-core-1-ch5/q03-fig-1.png\" alt=\"Figure 1: a circle centred at the origin O on x and y axes; the upper half, above the x-axis, is shaded and labelled R\"></figure><p>Figure 1 shows a circle with radius <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\"></span> and centre at the origin.<br>The region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>, shown shaded in Figure 1, is bounded by the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis and the part of the circle for which <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y&gt;0\"></span><br>The region R is rotated through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"360^\\circ\"></span> about the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis to create a sphere with volume <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\"></span></p><p>Use integration to show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V=\\dfrac43\\pi r^3\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p>",
